    "created_at": "2026-02-16T08:15:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-16T08:15:30Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the feedback! On the “descending range” case like age in [10, 5], my thought is that we should reject it during validation because it’s almost certainly a user mistake and silently accepting it makes the semantics ambiguous (is it an empty set, or should it be auto-normalized to [5, 10]?). If we do want to support it, I’d suggest we either clearly define it as invalid and return a consistent IllegalParam, or explicitly normalize it to [5, 10] and document the behavior. Personally I lean toward rejecting with a clear error message to avoid surprising results and to keep expression semantics strict and predictable.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
